# mutgap4_sys_iosfc_plane_size_v1: A plane's size reaches the IOSurface as kIOSurfacePlaneSize: one-plane 16x8 BGRA surfaces (a good plane, bytesPerRow 64) whose plane size is 256 (less than its rows), 512 (its rows) and 1024 (with an allocation of 1024), v1 and v2, each mapped then tested; each status and data page is locked. Measured: the 256-byte plane is refused (BadArgument, the test too, the page untouched); the others map and the test writes the allocation.
